WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.840
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Gotham we got a major reference to Bane

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.380
and Venom from the comics as well as the darker
corners of Wayne Enterprises.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:14.350
So just like normal I’ll start with my top
5 comic book moments and the do my review.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.680
Hello any new people.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.030
If you’re just finding me for the first
time, I’m doing all the DC TV shows, so

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.330
be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.960
It’s a really awesome time for comic book
tv right now.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.030
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.360
Here we go.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.809
Number 5 - Wayne Enterprises is Vast and somewhat
corrupt

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.870
The real villains here are the board members.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.819
At this point they’re the faceless power
behind Viper and Venom.

00:00:38.819 --> 00:00:42.179
There’s this really interesting relationship
between the super wealthy people in Gotham

00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:45.390
and the big mobsters like Falcone and Maroni.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:50.069
Some of the villains operate at night, some
during the day in an office.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:51.070
But they’re all bad.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:56.749
I don’t know if they specifically intended
to draw any references, but think of the Wayne

00:00:56.749 --> 00:00:58.409
Board Members as a Nest of Vipers.

00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:04.159
And yes, I do think that Wellzyne person at
the end is connected to one or more of the

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:05.159
board members.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:08.439
I don’t think she was working for Falcone
or Maroni.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:13.060
Someone we haven’t met yet.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:21.210
And don’t forget that a lot of the movies
and tv shows have sprung supervillains from

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.729
inside Wayne Enterprises.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:38.679
In 

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:46.179
the movies, The Riddler worked for Bruce Wayne
and I’m pretty sure Wayne also owned Axis

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:49.039
chemicals where the Michael Keaton Joker was
created.

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:53.680
I think in the comics the name was ACE Chemicals
and it was the Kane family that owned it.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.649
The Kane family is where Bruce’s Mother
comes from, her maiden name was Martha Kane.

00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:04.840
In the comics they own everything the Wayne’s
didn’t already own pretty much.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:13.770
So when she married Thomas Wayne it was like
the two richest people ever getting together.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.670
I don’t know if Gotham is going to address
the Kane family.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.980
But Gordon’s former fiancee Barbara is a
Kean, and they’re another super rich family.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.970
Number 4 - The Russian Mob

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.430
In the comics the Russian Mob has worked a
lot with Black Mask.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:33.310
On the show it seems like the Russian is just
a puppet in Mooney’s coup against Falcone.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.940
There was a man in a mask in the Halloween
promo the ran after the episode, but I don’t

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.790
think it’s going to be black mask.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.080
The big thing on the show has been showing
people before they became the big comic book

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.080
characters.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.060
Number 3 - Gotham University

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.790
This appeared in the comics for the first
time in 1941.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:55.560
In more recent years it’s where Batgirl
goes to school when she’s not fighting crime.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:06.730
There was also another student who became
Bat-Devil and a new version of Azrael.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.070
Bruce is way too young on the show to go there
now, but it’s possible for them to say that

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.720
some batman villains work there or are students.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.440
The big origin locations for batman villains
on the show are probably going to be Arkham,

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.870
Wayne Enterprises and Gotham U.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:24.950
Number 2 - World’s Greatest Detective

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.360
Bruce is supposed to be somewhere between
11 and 13 on the show.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.860
I give them a blanket pass on how clever he’s
allowed to be.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:35.640
Batman isn’t a genius, he’s just intelligent
and never stops working.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.850
He’s like the king of homework.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.840
Or Detective work.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.000
Almost the same thing.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.430
Two of my favorite scenes in the episode were
when he was first putting together his evidence

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.430
chart.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.720
I guess he hasn’t commissioned his super
computer yet.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.470
And at the end when Alfred joins him really
excitedly.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.370
Like Alfred finally gets that this is something
important for Bruce to do.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.330
Batman is a bit of an obsessive compulsive
when it comes to solving mysteries, so they

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.580
might take the character there this season.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.220
Like make him go a little nuts pushing himself
too hard.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.720
Alfred’s role is really to balance him out
emotionally.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.640
Like slap him back to sanity when he gets
too crazy.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:17.370
and my Number 1 comic book moment - Venom

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:28.470
They said it was stable in the episode, so
Wellzyne has a working formula.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:32.410
I think the question now is what is the show
going to do with it.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.730
Maybe nothing right now.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:46.540
Venom gets into Bane from the comics and I
don’t see the show doing him any time soon.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:50.670
The villains of this episode were trying to
show people how awful it was.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.880
In a really misguided crackpot way.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.910
I think there’s someone on the Wayne Board
that’s controlling Wellzyne though and they’ll

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.240
be one of the bigger villains this season.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.900
It’s possible the Wayne’s murder, Arkham
City and Wellzyne are all connected.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.620
There’s still a lot of characters the show
needs to introduce, so we’ll have a better

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:11.330
picture for who all the players are by the
middle of the season in a couple weeks.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.420
Let me know what your favorite moment was
though and what did you think of the Viper

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.420
special effects.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:19.420
They kind of reminded me of the Venom effects
from the Batman and Robin movie, with Bane’s

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.700
body twisting and growing.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.910
There were a few other easter eggs I spotted
to:

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.260
Bruce Wayne being into old Zorro flicks.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.280
Masked man and all.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.630
And Bette Kane.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.210
She was supposed to be in the episode, or
people were saying she was.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:44.360
She was the original Bat Girl in the comics,
and imdb is listing Sara Paxton in 17 episodes.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.640
There are only going to be 22 episodes this
season.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:55.520
So I guess she’ll be on the show next week
unless there’s some kind of error or something

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.480
big has changed.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:03.280
Overall I gave the episode a B, I felt like
the Bruce Detective story line was the strongest.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.790
The Venom parts got a little bit silly but
I think it will turn into something much much

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.760
bigger once we learn who the board members
are.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:27.300
I think the gallon of milk challenge 

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:38.880
was a clear sign that we were supposed to
laugh a little.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.990
We also saw a lot more David Mazouz, I like
his version of public Bruce Wayne.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:48.220
There’s the public persona he takes on when
he’s being Bruce Wayne Billionaire and then

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.740
there’s the Detective persona when he’s
being Batman.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:07:13.470
That’s why he seemed so patient with the
Wellzyne woman when he asked about the Board.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.990
He was just playing it cool.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:28.540
The catwoman scene felt a little out of place
and I feel like they could have tightened

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:34.169
things by just cutting out that food truck.

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:37.830
It still feels like they’re spending a lot
of time setting up big arcs.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.830
They want us to feel like Mooney versus Falcone
will be a big title fight and visually that

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.030
final scene was amazing.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.590
But I don’t feel like Mooney or her girl
on the inside are very threatening.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.651
It’s hard to stand out as a batman villain
if you’re not wearing clown makeup and randomly

00:07:50.651 --> 00:07:51.940
slicing people’s mouths open.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:08:31.599
Next week is going to be a halloween episode,
so I have high hopes for some craziness.

